[step] Specified two-colour lettering relief: the word rises 0.48 mm, two 0.24 mm layers, above the tile face. This step is the readable legend and its colour-change plane.
alternatives: Making the word flush removes the raised legend. A taller word changes the accepted two-layer label process and its relief; extending the whole tile face to the word plane removes the contrast boundary.
